hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24141","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah, meaning Ibn Kuhayl, from Muawiyah ibn Suwayd, he said: I slapped a freedman of ours, and his father said to him: Retaliate. Then he said: We, the company of Banu Muqarrin, were seven, we had no servant except one, one of us slapped her, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Free her. It was said to him: They have no servant other than her. He said: Let her serve them, and when they are independent of her, let them free her."
"24142","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, he said: We used to sell milk in the house of Suwayd ibn Muqarrin. He said: A slave-girl of Suwayd went out, spoke to a man of us, insulted him, and he slapped her face. Suwayd said: You slapped her; I have seen myself when I was the seventh of seven of my brothers, we had only a servant, one of us set upon her and slapped her, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us to free her."
"24143","Hushaym narrated to us, Husayn informed us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, that a man was staying in the house of Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, he said, and he slapped a servant. He said: Suwayd became angry and said: Did you find but the honor of his face? I have seen myself when we were the seventh of seven of the children of Muqarrin, and we had no servant except one, one set upon him and slapped him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered us when we return to free him, so we freed him."
"24144","Rawh narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, he said: I heard Hilal, a man from Banu Mazin, narrating from Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with nabidh in a jar, asked him, and he forbade me from it, so I broke it."
